# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in real values.
# `.env` itself is git-ignored — see ../.gitignore — so it never gets
# pushed. This file (.env.example) has no secrets in it and is safe
# to commit.

# --- Knowledge Engine bridge -------------------------------------------
# Only needed if SellerOS/ (the Knowledge Engine project) is NOT sitting
# right next to sellersos_tool_and_agent_layer_1/ on disk. Leave unset
# to use the default sibling-folder layout.
# SELLEROS_KNOWLEDGE_ENGINE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/SellerOS

# --- Amazon SP-API (for when amazon_connector.py moves off Mock Mode) --
# AMAZON_CLIENT_ID=
# AMAZON_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AMAZON_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# --- Flipkart Seller API (auto-switches connector from Playwright to API) --
# Leave all three unset/blank -> flipkart_connector uses Playwright
# (Seller Hub automation) automatically. Fill in all three once your
# API access is approved -> it switches to the real API automatically,
# on the next process restart, with no code changes needed anywhere.
# FLIPKART_CLIENT_ID=
# FLIPKART_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FLIPKART_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# --- Dev/single-seller MarketplaceSession (connectors/session_store.py) --
# Until real per-seller auth exists (backend team), this is how a
# MarketplaceSession actually gets built for local runs/testing.
# Read by connectors/session_store.py as a fallback whenever no
# session has been session_store.register()'d in memory for a given
# seller_id — good enough for one dev seller, not for production
# multi-tenant use. Amazon needs nothing here (Mock Mode connector).
# MEESHO_USERNAME=
# MEESHO_PASSWORD=
# FLIPKART_USERNAME=
# FLIPKART_PASSWORD=
